# LawApp - Core Context

UK employment-law AI platform. The server databases are the first line of every
answer. The LLM is a gated feeder that proposes content for verification before
it reaches the authoritative store. Local Ollama is the default model; no
external LLM on legal paths.

Stack: FastAPI backend; Postgres (corpus + pgvector) and operational Postgres;
Redis; service mesh on ports 8000 (monolith + UI), 8016 rules, 8017 RAG,
8018 graph-RAG, 8019 redaction, 8020 audit, 8007 admin, 8008 case, 8009 notify.
Graph layer is Postgres (`legal_nodes` / `legal_edges`), not Neo4j.

Fixed Kubernetes namespaces, never invent new ones:
`lawapp-api`, `lawapp-rag`, `lawapp-ai`, `lawapp-security`, `lawapp-monitoring`.

Invariants, never violate:
- The legal entity table is `matter`, not `case` (reserved word). `matter`
  bridges and replaces the legacy `cases` over time; do not keep dual tables
  synced forever.
- Provisions are temporally versioned. Every legal query filters by an as-at date.
- Every served answer or document carries a source citation and a
  verified / unverified badge.
- 16 canonical modules plus a subtopic / tag layer. Map the 24 `employment_modules`
  keys onto them; do not destructively replace and do not add modules without
  instruction.
- Coverage shown to users is honest and human ("Ready to read" / "Coming soon"),
  never internal states ("production" / "partial") and never "0 corpus excerpts".
  Do not claim 16-module coverage while the beta is 11 topics.

Authoritative specs live in `/docs`. Read them before large changes.
Style: hyphens, not em dashes, everywhere.
